  "problem": "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+2{x}^{2}).$\n\n$\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+2{x}^{2})=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,4{x}^{8}+\u22ef$",
  "worked_solution": "The Maclaurin series for $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $2{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+2{x}^{2}) & =(2{x}^{2})-\\frac{1}{2}(2{x}^{2})^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(2{x}^{2})^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(2{x}^{2})^{4}+\u22ef \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(4{x}^{4})+\\frac{1}{3}(8{x}^{6})-\\frac{1}{4}(16{x}^{8})+\u22ef \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{4}+\\frac{8{x}^{6}}{3}-4{x}^{8}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
